Alternative expected outputs (*_N.out) and the reason for each:

plllvm_cache_1.out: under debug_discard_caches every call rebuilds a call
site, so the counters of prepares read f (make installcheck-discard).

Messages of LLVM itself (parser, verifier) appear only in plllvm_jit and
plllvm_validator; another LLVM major may need _1.out files for these two.

A function's entry is revalidated by the xmin and ctid of its pg_proc row
alone.  Call sites are invalidated by PROCOID, NAMESPACEOID, AUTHMEMROLEMEM,
AUTHOID and DATABASEOID callbacks; under debug_discard_caches only the site counters
of plllvm_cache change, and make installcheck-discard checks that
plllvm_calls does not.

make installcheck-discard runs only the tests above.  plllvm_spi would not
fit there: its statements are replanned at every execution, and its
2000-call cases take minutes.
